        "diff": "--- /dev/null\n+++ /home/agent/workspace/spec.txt\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+Specification: abs — Absolute Value of an Integer\n+\n+1. Overview\n+    abs is a total function on the integers Z, mapping each integer to a\n+    non-negative integer.\n+\n+2. Signature\n+    abs : Z -> Z\n+\n+3. Definition\n+    For all x in Z:\n+\n+        abs(x) =  x   if x >= 0\n+        abs(x) = -x   if x <  0\n+\n+4. Expected Properties\n+    For all integers x:\n+\n+        P1 (Non-negativity):  abs(x) >= 0\n+        P2 (Identity case):   abs(x) =  x    if x >= 0\n+        P3 (Negation case):   abs(x) = -x    if x <  0\n+\n+5. Notes\n+    - P1 follows from P2 and P3, since both branches return a\n+      non-negative value for every x in Z.\n+    - abs is idempotent: abs(abs(x)) = abs(x) for all x in Z.\n+    - abs(x) = 0 if and only if x = 0.\n"
